<section class="unwritten-rules" aria-labelledby="rules-heading">
    <h2 id="rules-heading">Unwritten Rules of Our Team</h2>
    
    <div class="rules-grid">
        <!-- Rule 1 -->
        <article class="rule-card">
            <img src="~/images/rules/collaboration.webp" 
                 alt="Team members collaborating around a whiteboard" 
                 class="rule-image" 
                 width="400" height="260" 
                 loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <div class="rule-content">
                <span class="rule-badge">01</span>
                <h3>Assume Positive Intent</h3>
                <p>Start every conversation believing everyone is trying their best. It changes how you listen, respond, and build trust.</p>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Rule 2 -->
        <article class="rule-card">
            <img src="~/images/rules/communication.webp" 
                 alt="Two colleagues having a focused one-on-one conversation" 
                 class="rule-image" 
                 width="400" height="260" 
                 loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <div class="rule-content">
                <span class="rule-badge">02</span>
                <h3>Default to Transparency</h3>
                <p>Share context, not just conclusions. When people understand the "why," they make better decisions without asking permission.</p>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Rule 3 -->
        <article class="rule-card">
            <img src="~/images/rules/ownership.webp" 
                 alt="Person taking notes while reviewing project metrics" 
                 class="rule-image" 
                 width="400" height="260" 
                 loading="lazy" decoding="async">
            <div class="rule-content">
                <span class="rule-badge">03</span>
                <h3>Own the Gap</h3>
                <p>If something falls between roles, step into it. Flag it, fix it, or delegate it clearly. "Not my job" kills momentum.</p>
            </div>
        </article>
    </div>
